indications_original:
AMIDATE is indicated by intravenous injection for the induction of general anesthesia. When considering use of AMIDATE, the usefulness of its hemodynamic properties (see 
                        CLINICAL PHARMACOLOGY
                     ) should be weighed against the high frequency of transient skeletal muscle movements (see 
                        ADVERSE REACTIONS
                     ).
                  Intravenous AMIDATE is also indicated for the supplementation of subpotent anesthetic agents, such as nitrous oxide in oxygen, during maintenance of anesthesia for short operative procedures such as dilation and curettage or cervical conization.
